"""Replace the former library activity with a complete Construct workshop."""
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

def library(root):
    labs = root / 'labs'
    path = labs / 'library-lab.html'
    s = BeautifulSoup(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'), 'html.parser')
    s.title.string = 'Construct workshop: make your scene respond | DIKULT105'
    for script in s.select('script:not([src^="accessibility"])'): script.decompose()
    main = s.select_one('main')
    main.clear()
    main.append(BeautifulSoup('''<article class="reader" id="library-construct">
<p><a href="lab-programme.html#mapping-first-contact">Back to Construct first contact</a></p>
<p class="eyebrow">CONSTRUCT WORKSHOP / CONTINUE YOUR PROJECT</p><h1>Make your scene respond.</h1>
<p>You already made a tap reveal a thought. Now build a second response and decide how the two discoveries work together. Keep the same .c3p project and work in Construct beside this guide.</p>
<section class="step" id="construct-open"><p class="eyebrow">01 / RETURN TO YOUR SCENE</p><h2>Start with the response that works.</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="https://editor.construct.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Construct 3</a>. Choose Menu &gt; Project &gt; Open and open your saved .c3p.</li><li>In the Project Bar, expand Layouts and open your map.</li><li>Use Preview layout. Tap the object that reveals HiddenThought. Check that it works, then return to editing.</li><li>Save a separate copy, such as <code>my-scene-next.c3p</code>.</li></ol>
<figure class="official-shot"><a href="setup-assets/construct-interface.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="setup-assets/construct-interface.png" loading="lazy" alt="Real Construct editor with Properties at left, layout in the middle and Project Bar at right."/></a><figcaption>Actual Construct manual screenshot of a blank project. Find the layout at marker 5, Properties at 6 and Project Bar at 7. Your map appears in the middle. <a href="https://www.construct.net/en/make-games/manuals/construct-3/overview/the-interface" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original source</a>. Select to enlarge.</figcaption></figure>
<details><summary>I do not have the first response yet.</summary><p>Use <a href="lab-programme.html#mapping-first-contact">the first Construct walkthrough</a> to make one tap reveal HiddenThought, then return here.</p></details></section>
<section class="step" id="construct-plan"><p class="eyebrow">02 / TWO PLACES, TWO DISCOVERIES</p><h2>Choose another thing to uncover.</h2><p>Choose a second visible object in your scene. Give it a different message: a memory, a clue, a rumour or another character's perspective.</p><p>For example, the entrance reveals “I always arrive too early.” The garden reveals “Someone has been waiting here.” Use your own places and words.</p><p>Point to both tap targets and decide which sentence each should reveal.</p></section>
<section class="step" id="construct-build"><p class="eyebrow">03 / BUILD THE SECOND RESPONSE</p><h2>One new message. One new rule.</h2><ol><li>Double-click empty space in the layout. Search for Text and insert a new object type. Name it <code>SecondThought</code>, separate from HiddenThought.</li><li>Place it inside the map. Set its Text property to your second sentence. Turn Initially visible off. Make the box wide enough to read.</li><li>Click empty space in the layout. Read its Event sheet property and open that sheet from the Project Bar.</li><li>Click Add event. Choose Touch &gt; On tap object, select the second visible object and confirm.</li><li>On that new row, choose Add action &gt; SecondThought &gt; Set visible. Choose Visible and confirm.</li><li>Preview layout. Tap each target. Each should reveal its own message.</li></ol>
<figure class="official-shot"><a href="setup-assets/construct-events.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="setup-assets/construct-events.png" loading="lazy" alt="Actual Construct event sheet with condition at left, action at right and Add action on the same row."/></a><figcaption>Real manual example: System / On start of layout changes Text. Your rule has the same structure, with Touch / On tap object at left and SecondThought / Set visible at right. This shows the controls, not your finished tap rule. <a href="https://www.construct.net/en/make-games/manuals/construct-3/interface/event-sheet-view" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original source</a>. Select to enlarge.</figcaption></figure>
<p><strong>Test from the beginning:</strong> reload Preview. Both messages should start hidden.</p><details><summary>The wrong message appears, or both appear together.</summary><p>Check the object named in each action. The first rule should show HiddenThought, the second SecondThought. Two instances of the same Text object type can both be affected by Set visible. Use a separate object type for each message.</p></details></section>
<section class="step" id="construct-choice"><p class="eyebrow">04 / CHANGE THE EXPERIENCE</p><h2>Show one thought at a time.</h2><p>Make the latest discovery replace the previous one.</p><ol><li>On the first tap row, keep the action that shows HiddenThought. Add another action on the same row: SecondThought &gt; Set visible &gt; Invisible.</li><li>On the second tap row, keep the action that shows SecondThought. Add HiddenThought &gt; Set visible &gt; Invisible.</li><li>Preview. Tap the first target, then the second, then the first again. Only the latest message should stay visible.</li></ol><p>You kept the tap conditions and changed the actions. Choose whether one message at a time or several messages together fits your story better.</p></section>
<section class="step" id="construct-test"><p class="eyebrow">05 / LET SOMEONE EXPLORE</p><h2>Can a visitor discover it?</h2><p>Give a partner the fresh preview. Let them explore before telling them where to tap. Watch what they try and whether they can read the responses.</p><p>Change one thing after the test: move a target, improve its label or reposition a message. Preview and try again. You can test the same path yourself if a partner is unavailable.</p><p>Save your .c3p. Keep a short note: <strong>Tapping ____ reveals ____. After testing, I changed ____. Next I want ____.</strong></p><a class="primary" href="lab-programme.html#construct-rooms">Continue: rooms and rules in Construct</a></section></article>''', 'html.parser'))
    main.select_one('article').wrap(s.new_tag('div', id='steps'))
    path.write_text(str(s), encoding='utf-8', newline='\n')
    for name in ['tools.html', 'lab-programme.html']:
        path = labs / name
        t = BeautifulSoup(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'), 'html.parser')
        for link in t.select('a[href^="library-lab.html"]'):
            link.clear()
            link.string = 'Construct workshop: make your scene respond'
        if name == 'lab-programme.html':
            old = t.select_one('#library-construct-next')
            if old: old.decompose()
            t.select_one('#mapping-first-contact').append(BeautifulSoup('<div class="look" id="library-construct-next"><h4>Continue: build a second response</h4><p>Keep this Construct project. Add another tap target and message, then choose how the responses work together.</p><a class="primary" href="library-lab.html#library-construct">Continue the Construct workshop</a></div>', 'html.parser').find())
        path.write_text(str(t), encoding='utf-8', newline='\n')
